WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:05.703
- The universe appears to
be 13.8 billion years old.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:10.863
Earth is like four and a
half billion years old.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.300
In another half billion years or so,

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:19.900
the sun will expand and
probably evaporate the oceans

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.500
and make life impossible on Earth

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.910
which means if it had taken
consciousness 10% longer

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.160
to evolve, it would
never had evolved at all.

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:29.833
Just 10% longer.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:36.370
And I wonder how many dead
one-planet civilizations

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.020
there are out there in the cosmos

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:41.040
that never made it to the other planet

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.580
and then ultimately extinguish themselves

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.663
or were destroyed by external factors.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:47.633
Probably a few.

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:50.113
Channeling Carl Sagan.

00:00:52.417 --> 00:00:54.167
"Look again at that dot.

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:57.884
"That's here, that's home, that's us.

00:00:57.884 --> 00:00:59.677
"On it, everyone you love,

00:00:59.677 --> 00:01:00.857
"everyone you know,

00:01:00.857 --> 00:01:02.907
"everyone you've ever heard of,

00:01:02.907 --> 00:01:07.117
"every human being who ever
was lived out their lives.

00:01:07.117 --> 00:01:09.167
"The aggregate of our joy and suffering,

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:10.707
"thousands of confident religions,

00:01:10.707 --> 00:01:12.967
"ideologies and economic doctrines.

00:01:12.967 --> 00:01:15.547
"Every hunter and forager,
every hero and coward,

00:01:15.547 --> 00:01:18.547
"every creator and
destroyer of civilization.

00:01:18.547 --> 00:01:19.973
"Every king and peasant,

00:01:19.973 --> 00:01:21.952
"every young couple in love,

00:01:21.952 --> 00:01:24.287
"every mother and father,

00:01:24.287 --> 00:01:27.333
"hopeful child, inventor and explorer.

00:01:28.507 --> 00:01:32.087
"Every teacher of morals,
every corrupt politician,

00:01:32.087 --> 00:01:36.957
"every superstar, every supreme leader,

00:01:36.957 --> 00:01:38.907
"every saint and sinner in the history

00:01:38.907 --> 00:01:40.387
"of our species lived there

00:01:40.387 --> 00:01:43.163
"on a mode of dust suspended in a sunbeam.

00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:46.287
"Our planet is a lonely spec

00:01:46.287 --> 00:01:48.897
"in the great enveloping cosmic dark.

00:01:48.897 --> 00:01:50.352
"In our obscurity,

00:01:50.352 --> 00:01:52.857
"in all this vastness, there is no hint

00:01:52.857 --> 00:01:54.067
"that help will come from elsewhere

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:56.107
"to save us from ourselves.

00:01:56.107 --> 00:01:57.927
"The Earth is the only world known so far

00:01:57.927 --> 00:01:59.187
"to harbor life.

00:01:59.187 --> 00:02:00.407
"There's nowhere else,

00:02:00.407 --> 00:02:01.507
"at least in the near future

00:02:01.507 --> 00:02:04.670
"to which our species could migrate."

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:06.049
This is not true.

00:02:06.049 --> 00:02:07.290
(chuckling)

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:08.933
This is false, Mars.

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:11.780
- And I think Carl Sagan
would agree with that.

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:14.400
He couldn't even imagine it at that time.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.200
So thank you for making the world dream

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.264
and thank you for talking
today, I really appreciate it.

00:02:19.264 --> 00:02:20.437
- Thank you.

